select '00b888dd-a366-519e-89ae-453c01dc939a', l.id, 1,
  'Nucléotide et nucléoside', 'Nucleotide and nucleoside', 'Nucléotide = pentose + phosphate + base ; nucléoside = pentose + base.', 'Nucleotide = pentose + phosphate + base; nucleoside = pentose + base.', 'https://kjlgrgdryimazczrcvgx.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/lesson-media/biologie/cytologie-i/ADN-ARN.jpg', 'https://kjlgrgdryimazczrcvgx.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/lesson-media/biologie/cytologie-i/ADN-ARN.jpg',
  'Un nucléotide est formé d''un pentose (ribose ou désoxyribose), d''un groupe phosphate et d''une base azotée. Un nucléoside ne contient que le pentose et la base, sans phosphate. Le pentose possède cinq atomes de carbone ; le glucose, lui, est un hexose.', 'A nucleotide is made of a pentose (ribose or deoxyribose), a phosphate group and a nitrogenous base. A nucleoside contains only the pentose and the base, with no phosphate. The pentose has five carbon atoms; glucose, by contrast, is a hexose.', 'De quoi est composé un nucléoside ?', 'What is a nucleoside made of?',
  'Pentose + base azotée', 'Pentose + nitrogenous base', 'Nucléoside = sucre + base ; nucléotide = sucre + base + phosphate.', 'Nucleoside = sugar + base; nucleotide = sugar + base + phosphate.', 'Le nucléoside n''a pas de phosphate ; l''ajout du phosphate donne le nucléotide.', 'A nucleoside has no phosphate; adding one makes a nucleotide.'
